      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>Can I do this 7-day itinerary in reverse (Fes to Marrakech)?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Running the route from Fes to Marrakech works just as well. The driving times and scenic stops remain the same. Starting in Fes allows you to begin in Morocco's quietest imperial medina and end with the lively rooftop restaurant scene in Marrakech.
      </p>

      <h3>Is it better to spend two nights in the desert or two nights in Marrakech?</h3>
      <p>
        For a 7-day trip, we strongly recommend two nights in the desert. Driving 8 to 10 hours out to Merzouga for a single 14-hour overnight visit is physically exhausting. Spending two full nights allows you to actually relax, see nomadic culture in Khamlia, and enjoy the silence of Erg Chebbi without rushing back into a vehicle the next morning. If you have 10 days, explore our <a href="/blog/morocco-10-day-itinerary.html"><strong>ultimate 10-day Morocco itinerary</strong></a> which gives you two full nights in both Marrakech and Fes.
      </p>

      <h3>What should I pack for this road trip?</h3>
      <p>
        Layers are essential. Because you travel from the warm Marrakech plains up over high mountain passes (2,260m) and out into desert flats, temperatures vary widely in a single day. Pack comfortable walking shoes for medina cobbles, light breathable cotton clothing for the day, a fleece or down jacket for cold desert evenings, sunglasses, and a wide-brim hat. Review our full guide on <a href="/blog/what-to-wear-in-morocco.html"><strong>what to wear in Morocco</strong></a>.
      </p>

